% Problem 39. Chace vol. II pl. 61 (photographs XVI-XVII, register 1), PDF pp. 169-170; Peet p. 77 (Pl. M).
No. 39
"{Example of} making the difference of share. Loaves 100 for man 10, 50 to 6, 50 to 4. What is the difference of share?"   % "tp n" (Example of) in red; Chace fn 1: twnw, "difference of share", more literally "excess" (Gunn)
% 50 loaves among 4 men: 4 is multiplied to find 50 (no sentence in the papyrus)
  1      4
\ 10     40
  2      8            % no tick in either edition; Peet: (sic)
\ '2     2
% 50 loaves among 6 men
  1      6
  2      12
  4      24
\ 8      48
\ '3     2
% the shares set out: four of 12 '2 in one column, six of 8 '3 beside them
"12 '2   8 '3"
"12 '2   8 '3"
"12 '2   8 '3"
"12 '2   8 '3"
"        8 '3"
"        8 '3"
"The difference of share is 4 '6."   % Peet: "No working of this step is shown" (12 '2 less 8 '3)
